DRY BY DEFAULT. With no --close the tool runs every gate and builds every payload in memory. It then prints one JSON
report: each gate met or unmet, and what --close would write, with byte counts and sha256. It writes nothing under
M8. `--dry-report DIR` also writes the previews to DIR, and refuses a DIR inside M8. `--close` performs the writes, and
only when every gate is met. OW-25 and OW-11 make closing, publication and campaign-log appends THE OWNER'S ACT: the
orchestrator runs this tool dry and never with --close.

WHAT IS RE-KEYED FROM LAMENTATIONS, AND WHY.
- The grader model is READ from campaign/grader_models.v1.json. The carrier's digest is pinned here. OW-25 forbids
  loosening the gate to accept any model, so the gate names the carrier's model.
- The Lam final-check gate reads one claude-fable-5-1 packet. This one reads BOTH blind lanes of the OW-26 merged-verdict
  close. Every lane must return postcheck fit_to_assemble, final check fit_to_close over this corpus's sha256, and
  items 20-23 fit_to_accept.
- The Lam stage-1 transcript-audit gate (packets + _final_check_reconcile.py) is NOT run. OW-26 recorded that audit as
  OWED, NOT MET. The gate here asserts the opposite of what Lam asserts: every lane's final check must say
  reconcile_verdict NOT_RUN, bytes_audited_by_stage1 0, and a statement that names the audit as OWED. The receipt
  carries transcript_audit "OWED, NOT MET". Nothing here can be read as that audit having run.
- The completion receipt must carry grader_fallback {model, statement}. The statement must be byte-equal to the
  carrier's downgrade statement (OW-25 receipt rule). It must also carry the OW-26 weakness statement from the same
  carrier.
- Lane outputs are read only from their durable transcriptions under merged_close/. The landing manifest lists them
  with sha256, and every file is re-hashed here. The scratch originals are not read.
- Tiling is proven contiguous over ezek_lib's WEB verse order: every row starts one verse after the last row ended, and
  the rows cover 1273 verses. This is stronger than Lam's sum.
- Packet retention: 1854 files, 119 MB, is too large to inline. It is a manifest file (path, bytes, sha256). The receipt
  carries that file's digest.
- The shared atlas feed: the Lam pattern appends 12-field rows derived from the sidecars. Ezekiel also has the item-22
  deliverable of 102 rows, which carries one judged 'high' row and four extra fields. Both paths would put Ezekiel rows
  in the same shared file, so --close requires an explicit --acf {lam_pattern,item22}. The dry report shows both.
  Choosing is the owner's act (OW-11), and appending both is refused.
  AMENDED 2026-09-23 (v9b): any --acf, dry or close, must meet checks/validate_book_review_coverage.py's per-book
  feed rule, measured here (one row per low/medium_low chunk and no other, each mirroring the chunk's span,
  confidence, review status and hold state). The dry report gives both options' coverage and the shared feed's
  existing shapes by book, so a question about the choice is sourced from the report.
  AMENDED 2026-09-23 (v9c): the gate also checks review_packet_final_state. The validator compares it with
  reviews/<book>/review_packets.jsonl, which no close tool from Job onward writes, so here it must be the state
  the chunk's hold implies (accepted_candidate when the hold is null, else held_lower_confidence).
  AMENDED 2026-09-23 (v9d): both stale tests apply only inside the low/medium_low set (v9c's bare `or` let the
  state test run on orphans too).

AMENDED 2026-09-23 (v9 fix round, OW-28). Both v1 merged-close lanes returned not_fit over rows_v8_final, each on one
medium (A: P03-001 F-414; B: P06-015 SIGNAL_OUT_OF_SPAN). A bounded fix round built rows_v9_final: three rows changed and
the rest are byte-identical to v8, per rows_v9_final.manifest.json. Two blind delta lanes then re-checked THE DELTA over
v9. So:
- CORPUS is v9. The lineage gates prove that v9 differs from v8 only in the (row, field) pairs the manifest lists.
- The v1 lanes' final checks must be over the BASE (v8). Their verdicts stand as recorded (not_fit). Every v1 residual
